    while ((fgets(buffPtr, sizeof(buffer), stdin)) != NULL && (strchr(buffPtr, '\n') != NULL)) {
        int len = strlen(buffPtr);
        memmove(buffer, buffPtr, len + 1); // copy the data to the original buffer
        bytesRead += len;
        buffPtr = &buffer[len];
    }
    return bytesRead;
}
```

This code defines a `scan` function that reads input from standard input until it encounters a newline character. The newline character is not stored in the buffer. The function returns the number of characters read.

